"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[15075],{15075:function(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"content":"\\n<center>\\n<BookCard \\n          cover=\\"/assets/snippets/books/the-heart-of-brutus.png\\"\\n          title=\\"The Heart of Brutus\\"\\n          author=\\"Keigo Higashino\\"\\n          publisher=\\"Random House Korea\\"\\n          publishedDate=\\"2007-08-04\\"\\n          isbn=\\"9788925511245\\"\\n          rating=3.5\\n          tags=\\"mystery\\"\\n        />\\n</center>\\n\\n## Review\\nThe entire work is woven together with the keyword <mark>betrayal</mark>.  \\nThere is a ```betrayal of conspiracy``` where the three conspirators cannot fully trust each other.  \\nThere is a ```betrayal of love``` where someone pursues their own interests while deceiving three men simultaneously.  \\nAnd the ```betrayal of insubordination``` forms the core of the case.  \\nFinally, at the peak of all these human betrayals, there is the ```betrayal by the creation```, the betrayal of the robot ```Brutus```.  \\n<br>\\nThis work progressively deepens the theme of betrayal, exposing the cynical truth that no human relationship can be anything but vulnerable in the face of selfishness.  \\n<br>\\nA work that stands out for its original and novel idea of a murder relay.  \\n<br>\\nEven though it is a work from 30 years ago, the questions about the ```relationship between technology and humanity``` posed by this novel come across as even more valid and chilling in modern society where AI and robot technology have entered our lives more deeply.  \\n<br>\\nThis work was warning ahead of its time what tragedy could result when human ethical awareness cannot keep up with the speed of technological development.  "}')}}]);